6 GHz

- Available with Wi-Fi 6E and Wi-Fi 7 devices.
- Offers additional spectrum and less congestion in supported regions.
- Generally requires closer proximity to the access point for optimal performance.

## Quick exam tip

Remember these associations:

- 802.11n = Wi-Fi 4
- 802.11ac = Wi-Fi 5
- 802.11ax = Wi-Fi 6 / 6E
- 802.11be = Wi-Fi 7

Also, 802.11 belongs to the IEEE 802.11 family of wireless LAN standards, which operates at the OSI physical and data link layers.

